    "durationMs": 623596,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Implementation** (Rails 8.0.2, API-only, Ruby 3.4.3, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`)\n- `POST /links` — validates absolute http/https URL with host, optional custom code (`/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$/`), generates unique 8-char codes when omitted; returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL echoed unchanged; 409 on duplicate code (race-safe via unique index + `RecordNotUnique` rescue), 422 on invalid input or malformed JSON\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with `{code, url, clicks}` or 404 JSON error\n- `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with Location set to the stored URL; click count incremented by one atomic SQL `UPDATE` per request; 404 JSON for unknown codes\n- `GET /links` — `{items, total}` in ascending creation order\n- Click counts and data live in PostgreSQL, so they survive restarts (verified: clicks persisted across a kill + restart, then incremented correctly)\n\n**Notable fixes along the way**\n- Bundler had resolved `json` 3.1.0, which removed the `quirks_mode` option Rails 8.0.2 still passes to `JSON.generate` — every `render json:` returned 500. Pinned `json` 2.9.1 in the Gemfile.\n- Added a fallback so a JSON body without a `Content-Type: application/json` header is still parsed.\n- `start.sh` runs `rails db:prepare` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; it installs nothing.\n\n**Validation** — a 36-assertion HTTP suite (all status codes, error bodies, URL echoing, generated-code format, ordering, click increments) passed 36/36 on a clean database, plus a restart-persistence check. The server is stopped, port 8000 is free, and the `links` table is empty and migrated, ready for the grading run."
  }
